  - m_Id: 11362644099227
    m_Localized: The Nile River flows from south to north.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099228
    m_Localized: The goddess Sekhmet has the head of a lion.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099229
    m_Localized: Pharaoh Tutankhamun ruled Egypt for less than 10 years.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099230
    m_Localized: Papyrus paper was invented in Egypt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099231
    m_Localized: The god in charge of the Nile River was called Sobek.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099232
    m_Localized: Egypt has a good track record with Karate.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099233
    m_Localized: Al Ahly SC is a football club from Egypt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099234
    m_Localized: Queen Nefertiti was the mother of Pharaoh Tutankhamun.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099235
    m_Localized: The ancient Egyptians were the originators of the 12-month calendar.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11362644099236
    m_Localized: The last pharaoh of ancient Egypt was Pharaoh Ramesses II.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
